  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "The equation of the circle, which touches the line $y=5$ and passes through $(-1,2)$ and $(1,2)$ is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "5PWVP",
      "text": "$9 x^{2}+9 y^{2}-60 y+75=0$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "Xbkxl",
      "text": "$9 x^{2}+9 y^{2}-60 x-75=0$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "q1UCb",
      "text": "$9 x^{2}+9 y^{2}+60 y-75=0$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "oMDhL",
      "text": "$9 x^{2}+9 y^{2}+60 x+75=0$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/bitsat/qSv62DZUInezs9OtYo4L1dI8LmR24DBWnsy_SoSgY6A.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\r\n\r\nThe centre of the circle is on the perpendicular bisector of the line joining $(-1,2)$ and $(1,2)$, which is the $y$-axis. The ordinate of the centre is given by\r\n\r\n$\\begin{array}{l}\r\n\r\n(5-y)^{2}=1+(y-2)^{2} \\\\\r\n\r\n\\Rightarrow y=\\frac{10}{3}\r\n\r\n\\end{array}$\r\n\r\nHence, eq. of the circle is:\r\n\r\n$\\begin{array}{l}\r\n\r\nx^{2}+\\left(y-\\frac{10}{3}\\right)^{2}=\\left(\\frac{5}{3}\\right)^{2} \\\\\r\n\r\n\\Rightarrow 9 x^{2}+9 y^{2}-60 y+75=0\r\n\r\n\\end{array}$",
    "image": null
  },
